@module screens ; The menu screens: the screen list, the screen switch, the help lines
@about The menus are a list of screens (ScreenList $74E6): each screen is a pair of words, the routine that draws it and its pointer zone table. SetScreen $7060 takes the Nth pair (E = 2N): the routine goes to the loop's return address ($6A99) and the zone table to PointerZones; the view flag ends the current loop.
$7040 c ScreenFour ; Remember key A, screen 2 (E = 4); the mission code's vector $67EE
> Witness: L1 9 (missions, play, play2).

$7047 c ScreenSix ; Remember key A, screen 3 (E = 6)
> Witness: known only from the code.

$704E c ScreenEight ; Remember key A, screen 4 (E = 8)
> Witness: L1 14 (missions, play, play2).

$7055 c ScreenFromClick ; Key "C", screen 0
> Witness: L1 15 (menu, missions, play, play2).

$705A c ScreenZero ; Screen 0 (E = 0)
> Witness: L1 91 (c1, death, m2erbe, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$705E c ScreenTwo ; Screen 1 (E = 2)
> Witness: L1 12 (menu, missions, play2).

$7060 c SetScreen ; Switch to entry E/2 of the screen list: the draw routine to $6A99, the zone table to $6D47
> Witness: L1 121 (c1, death, m2erbe, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$707E c SetViewFlag ; $6A6D = $FF: the current loop ends
> Witness: L1 10 (play, play2).

$7084 c ShowPauseOnce ; Once: bank 6's $DACB and $DB64, then patched to RET
> Witness: L1 10 (menu, play, play2).
$709E PrintTitleOnce

$70B6 c DragonflyTitle ; Once: bank 6's $C079, the title string at ($70A3), the attribute box $C0BB
> Witness: L1 1 (play).

@module catalogue ; The mission catalogue: the directory load, the text of a mission
$70C6 c CopyCatalogueHead ; Copy the catalogue's first 32 bytes to bank 6 $CF85 and the 1 K from $CB84 to the back buffer
> Pages bank 4, copies `$CB64` (32 bytes) via `$8AF1` to bank 6 `$CF85`, then `$CB84` (1024 bytes) to `$8AF1`. Witness: L1 32 (menu, missions, search).

$70F6 c CopyMissionText ; Copy mission ($757D)'s texts from the catalogue (bank 4) to bank 6 $DBF3
> Record n of the 8-byte index at `$CCA6`: the offset, two words stored at `$7143` and `$7151`, the end; the text is copied through `$8AF1` to `$DBF3`; `$70A3` and `$7C55` get the addresses of its two parts. Witness: L1 25 (menu, missions, search).

$715D c LoadDirectory ; Load the catalogue from side 2: the 17-byte header "DIRECTORY", then its block to bank 4 $CB64
> Loops until a header whose name is "DIRECTORY" (`$71B3`) loads, prints `$C90D` ("loading"), pages bank 4 and loads the block (length from the header `$8AFC`) to `$CB64`; retries until its first 9 bytes are "MISSION:T" (`$71BB`). Witness: L1 13 (c1, menu, missions, search).

$719B c PrintRewind ; Print bank 6 $C93E
> Witness: L1 25 (c1, menu, missions, search).

