$74E6 b ScreenList 2 ; The menu screens: the current pointer, then pairs of words (draw routine, zone table)
> Read and moved by `SetScreen` `$7060`.

$757C c ScreenOfMission ; Screen 1 unless the current mission ($757D) is $FF or not completed
> `LD A,n`: n (`$757D`) is the mission the tape gave (`$8528`: the header's digit - "1"). Witness: L1 10 (play).
$757D CurrentMission ; the operand: the mission number 0-9 ($FF none)

$7588 c MissionLoaded ; If a mission is loaded: bank 6 $CBF4, $D27C, $CA23, then screen 0
> Witness: known only from the code (entered by a jump from `$75B8`).

$759A c LoadMissionIfAllowed ; Load the mission the tape holds; mission 10 only when the nine completion flags are set
> If the current mission (C) is 9 (Grand Finale), the nine bytes `$6799-$67A1` are ANDed: if any is 0 the mission is refused (`RET Z`, recording m10: the status screen). Otherwise `LoadMission` `$84C1`. Witness: L1 18 (m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, missions).

$75BB c MissionDone ; A = the completion flag of the current mission ($6799 + n): NZ when done
> Witness: L1 28 (m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, missions, play).

$75CA w IconTable 2 ; The addresses of the 19 weapon icons (bank 6), read by DrawIcon
> 19 words at `$75CA-$75EF`: icon n at word n-1.

$75F0 b ObjectTable 30 ; The 24 object records, 60 bytes each: 0 the player, 1-20 the mission's objects, 21 the Helicarrier, 22-23 projectiles
> +0 list index, +1 type, +2 state (bit 7 present, 6 wreck, 5 drawn, 2 on the radar), +3 handler flags, +4 colour, +5 height, +7 speed, +8 wreck model, +`$0B` box half-sizes, +`$13` hit points, +`$14` damage, +`$16` radius, +`$18` step handler, +`$1A` collision handler, +`$1C` model, +`$1E` score, +`$22` heading, +`$23` X (24 bits), +`$26` Y (24 bits), +`$2A` pitch, +`$2B` view position, +`$31` timer, +`$32` AI state, +`$3B` collision slot. Bytes +1 to +`$1E` come from the type's template. Read by RunObjectHandlers `$C026`, written by the world code (frag of bank 2 / 0, docs 05-07).
> Witness: every play build reads and writes `$75F0-$7B8F`.
$75F5 PlayerHeight
$75F7 PlayerSpeed
$7608 PlayerHandler
$7612 PlayerHeading
$7613 PlayerX
$7616 PlayerY
$7ADC HelicarrierRecord

$7B90 b PlayWorkspace 16 ; The per-store-type table and play variables, then the interrupt's stack (top $7C49) and the fuel word $7C57
> `$7B89` + 8 x type (type 1-13, from `$7B91`): the aim, fire and select routines of each weapon store; `$7BF9` the failure reason text pointer; the interrupt handler's stack below `$7C49`; `$7C57` the fuel (reset to `$3F00` by bank 6 `$CC1B`).
$7BF9 FailReason
