@module text
$7C59 b SmallFont 5 ; The small font: 44 glyphs "0" to "[", 5 rows of a byte each, ink 0 (the glyphs are stored inverted)
> Read by SmallGlyph `$6DDA` (HL = `$7C59` + 5 (code - "0")) for the panel's numbers and short words; the 5 pixels a row are the high bits, the low three always 1. Witness: every read build (185 of the 220 bytes read; "@", ":", "<" ... never).
@res fonts/small-font.bin

$7D35 b SmallFontLeftover 16 ; 28 bytes after the font that no routine reads or writes (leftover of an earlier build)

@module interrupt ; The IM 2 handler and the jobs it runs every frame
@about The handler $8383 runs at every interrupt (the 257 vectors at $8200 all give $8383): it switches to its own stack (top $7C49 in bank 5), saves every register, and calls the tick routines: the sound ($7E6E bank 0), bank 4's tick, the mission clock, the warning blinkers, the keyboard, the pointer, the message timer; then in play (the flag $83BF) bank 6's display jobs, or in the menus the panel blits and the 3D view's blit (the routine in $83E6) when the frame is ready ($83BA).
$7D51 c SetMessage ; Store the message timer: the attribute (IY+3) to $7D64, the hook $7D5D enabled
> Witness: L1 61 (death, missions, play, play2).

$7D5D c MessageOnce ; Once: the timer $87D7 = 100, then the message of bank 0 ($D86B or $D84E) printed
> Patched to `RET` after one run. Witness: L1 3601 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$7D80 c PointerTick ; Read the controls, move the pointer within the screen, test the fire
> `ReadControls` `$971A`, the X and Y steps (`$985E`, `$985F`) added to the pointer (`$7DC0`, `$7DC1`) within 8-247 and 8-183, then `PointerFire` `$7DC2`. Witness: L1 69895 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).
$7DA7 ClampStep

$7DC0 b PointerPos 2 ; The pointer's X and Y (copied to $7C51 / $7C53 by $897E)

$7DC2 c PointerFire ; Carry (the fire) held: after 25 frames a click ($6D43 = $FF) at the pointer, repeated every 5
> Witness: L1 69895 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$7DFB c ClockTick ; The mission clock: every 50 interrupts one second on in $68EA (seconds, minutes, hours)
> A `NOP` while it runs; the mission header's loader puts `RET` here (`$8612`) until play. Witness: L1 69895 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$7E2C b LoadedMission 3 ; Two spare bytes and the mission loaded last ($7E2E, $FF none)
$7E2E LastLoadedMission

$7E2F b ClockText 11 ; The clock's string: position codes and "00:00", $FF

$7E3A c PrintClock ; Print the clock's minutes and hours ($68EB, $68EC) as two digit pairs
> Witness: L1 530 (play, play2).

$7E6E c SoundTick ; The interrupt's sound step: bank 0's driver $D692, the bank kept
> Witness: L1 69896 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$7E7A c ClearPointerState ; $66CE and the click flag cleared
> Witness: L1 2966 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$7E82 b MissionParams 12 ; 12 bytes of the mission header ($DBF1), copied by $8598

