$A422 c NearClipLineEnd ; The other end of a line behind the eye too: no carry (skip the line); else NearClipLine
> Witness: L1 266 (death, missions).

$A42B c NearClipLine ; Cut the 3D segment V[B] - V[B'] at the near plane by bisection and project the cut: carry, HL / HL' = the screen point
> Reads both ends with `$A4D1` / `$A4F1` (vertex + the object position operands), halves the segment until depth - 96 is 0, then projects the point (Divide `$A687`, DivideByLog `$A6D2`, NegHL `$A771`) like OpProject. `$67B2-$67B5` hold the depths being halved.
> Witness: L1 3110 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A4D1 c FetchVertexXY ; x + `$9A8E` of V[B] to `$A503`, y + `$9AB3` to HL
> Witness: L1 6220 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A4F1 c FetchVertexDepth ; z + `$9A6C` - 96 of the vertex: the signed distance to the near plane
> Witness: L1 6220 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A509 c ClipPolyNear ; Cut a face at the near plane (Sutherland-Hodgman on depth = 96) into PolyVerts `$6700`
> Walks the face's point offsets from IX; at each in / out change calls NearClipLine `$A42B` and appends the cut with AppendPolyVertex `$A677`. Returns carry = the polygon is complete (fill it), Z = go on with the next point, NZ = nothing left.
> Witness: L1 3987 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A677 c AppendPolyVertex ; Append (BC, DE) to the polygon list at HL and count it in `$66D5`
> Witness: L1 4168 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A687 c Divide ; HL = 256 HL / DE (signed HL, positive DE) by logarithms; DE = log2 of the divisor, kept for a second DivideByLog
> Normalises DE to an 8-bit mantissa and an exponent, looks up LogFraction / LogInteger `$5C00`, then falls into DivideByLog. 283 939 calls (11 recordings).
> Witness: L1 283939 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A6D2 c DivideByLog ; HL = 256 HL / 2^(DE / 256): log of |HL|, minus DE, antilog by ExpFraction `$5E00`, the sign back
> The shift of the 9-bit mantissa is a self-patched `JR` into an `ADD HL,HL` chain (`$A739`, `$A75A`). A result below 1 gives 0 (`$A765`), an overflow `$3EE4` and carry (`$A769`). The most called 3D routine: 475 056 entries, 45 permille.
> Witness: L1 475056 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A745 c ApplySign ; Negate HL when the sign saved in F' is set
> Witness: L1 425915 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A765 c ZeroQuotient ; HL = 0
> Witness: L1 24493 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A771 c NegHL ; HL = -HL
> Witness: L1 308008 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A779 c Random ; A = a pseudo-random byte: two additive words patched in place mixed with R (the mission vector `$67D0`)
> Witness: L1 584 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A799 c AbsA ; A = |A| (the mission vector `$67D6`)
> Witness: L1 179580 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A79E c NegDE ; DE = -DE
> Witness: L1 2228 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A7A6 c NegAbsHL ; HL = -|HL|
> Witness: known only from the code (no recording runs it).

$A7AB c AbsHL ; HL = |HL|
> Witness: L1 2 (play).

$A7AE c NegateHL ; HL = -HL (the mission vector `$67D3`)
> Witness: L1 18194 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A7B6 c HighTimes32 ; HL = H * 32 (the back-buffer row offset of row H)
> Witness: L1 71059 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A7B7 c LowTimes32 ; HL = L * 32
> Witness: L1 72315 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A7BF c MulSigned ; HL = A * E, signed bytes, by quarter squares: ((A+E)^2 - A^2 - E^2) / 2
> When A + E overflows it uses A^2 + E^2 - (A-E)^2 (`$A7DD`). Tables SquareLow / SquareHigh `$5F00`.
> Witness: L1 107436 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A7F2 c MulFrac ; HL = A * E / 128 rounded, signed bytes: the product with a sine of Sine8
> Witness: L1 66079 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A82C c MulWordByte ; HL = HL * A / 128 for a signed word HL and a signed byte A (two quarter-square products)
> The mission vector `$67D9`: 220 482 calls in play, 37 permille, most of them from the mission code turning positions.
> Witness: L1 220482 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A899 c SinCos8 ; A = Sine8[A], A' = Sine8[A + 64] (the mission vector `$67E8`)
> Witness: L1 58907 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$A8A5 c SinCos16 ; DE = Sine16[A], BC = Sine16[A + 64]
> Witness: L1 4970 (c1, death, missions, play, play2).

$A8B2 c SinCosHalf ; E = A = sine, A = cosine of the angle word HL (H the angle, bit 7 of L the half step: Sine8Half `$6400`)
> Witness: L1 22941 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

@module player ; The player's tank: steering, fuel, armour, terrain and boundary checks, the weapons and their projectiles
@about The player is record 0 ($75F0): speed $75F7, heading $7612, X $7613-$7615, Y $7616-$7618, height $75F5, step handler $7608 (PlayerStep $A8C7), collision handler PlayerHit $CAA5. Fuel $7C57, armour $8301-$8303 (sides) and $8304 (top), the four loaded weapon slots $8368 (6 bytes: +0 store type, +5 ammunition), the current slot $C53C.
$A8C7 c PlayerStep ; The player's step handler: terrain, boundary, fuel, the turret
> Record 0's step handler (+$18 = `$A8C7`, run by RunObjectHandlers `$C026` with IX = `$75F0`). Calls TerrainCollision through `$67F1`; on a hit the terrain type `$CE69` decides: 2 or `$80` (a wall) negates the speed and sets the handler to BounceDecay `$CC09`; 0 or 6 (rough ground) slows the speed by a quarter. Then BoundaryCheck `$D4B8`, then the fuel: `$7C57` -= (|speed| >> 4) OR 1; on an underflow `$A94E` sets the failure reason `$7BF9` = `$CCED` ("RAN OUT OF FUEL") and calls `$7047`. The Infinite Fuel POKE writes 42 at `$A958` (`LD ($7C57),HL` becomes `LD HL,($7C57)`). Then the turret and speed against the control state `$985F`.
> Witness: L1 3503 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).
$A94E OutOfFuel ; fuel underflow: $7BF9 = $CCED "RAN OUT OF FUEL", CALL $7047 (static, no recording ran out of fuel)
$A958 ; the Infinite Fuel POKE writes 42 here

$A986 c PlayerSteering ; Steering and the fire key: heading += turn / 2, the fire cooldown
> Adds half the turn input `$985E` to the heading `$7612`; counts down the fire cooldown `$A9FD`; when it is zero and the fire key bit of `$6D43` is set, calls the current weapon's fire routine through the operand at `$A9B9` (set from the store-type table `$7B89` + 8 * type, word 3). Output: a projectile record, the cooldown restarted.
> Witness: L1 3521 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$A9C9 b PlayerSteeringTail 8 ; The rest of PlayerSteering that no recording runs (the speed clamp)
> Code bytes after the branch the recordings take in PlayerSteering: `LD A,(IX+7)` / `ABS` through `$67D6`, stores `$7E8E`, the clamp against 8. Kept as bytes because the walk does not reach it from a run.

$A9F7 c SetFireCooldown ; Set the fire cooldown to 8 passes
> Writes 8 to the cooldown byte `$A9FD`, the delay before the next shot. Called by the fire routines after a launch.
> Witness: L1 69 (death, play, play2).

$A9FD b FireCooldown 1 ; The fire cooldown, passes until the next shot
> Counted down by PlayerSteering `$A986`, set by SetFireCooldown `$A9F7`.

@module objects ; The object table: 24 records of 60 bytes, spawning from the mission list, transform, depth sort, collisions, radar
@about ObjectTable $75F0 (bank 5): 24 records of 60 bytes; record 0 is the player, 1-20 the general slots, 21 ($7ADC) the Helicarrier, 22-23 weapons. +1 type, +2 state flags (bit7 present, bit6 wreck, bit2 on the radar), +3 handler flags (bit0 step handler on), +5/+6 height, +7 speed, +$13 hit points, +$14 damage, +$16/+$17 radius, +$18/+$19 step handler, +$1A/+$1B collision handler, +$1C/+$1D model, +$1E/+$1F score, +$22 heading, +$23-+$25 X, +$26-+$28 Y, +$31-+$3A per-type state, +$3B collision slot. The first 30 bytes after +1 come from the type's template.
$A9FE c PlotRadarPixel ; Plot one radar pixel through the row table $6600
> Input: the blip's x and y on the radar. Looks up the screen row in the table `$6600`, ORs the pixel mask (E = `$49` + x AND 7 gives the bit) into the screen at the radar window `$5036`. Called by DrawRadar `$C05E` for each blip in the list `$6768`.
> Witness: L1 14562 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

@module raster
$AA27 c PlotBackBuffer ; Set the pixel (x = L, y = H) in the back buffer (the bit masks at `$7C49`)
> Caller `$BB75` (points of the scenery). 37 012 calls.
> Witness: L1 37012 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

@module render
$AA47 c BoxSquareTurret ; BoxSquare with the second heading `$68E9` in place of `$68E7` (the mission vector `$67FD`): a turret
> Witness: L1 17 (missions).

$AA63 c BoxSquare ; Native (turn, size, height): the 8 corners V34-V41 of a square box turned by the heading `$68E7` + turn, V33 = 0
> With S = size sin(a) / 128 and C = size cos(a) / 128: V34 = (C, -h, -S), V35 = (S, -h, C), V36 = (-C, -h, S), V37 = (-S, -h, -C), V38-V41 the same at y = +h. The mission vector `$67F4`.
> Witness: L1 483 (c1, death, missions, play, play2).

$AAC2 c BoxHeights ; Last operand h: y = -h for V34-V37, +h for V38-V41; V33 = (0, 0, 0); return
> Witness: L1 9618 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$AAF5 c BoxRect16 ; Native (half angle, radius, height): a rectangle box with 16-bit corners (Sine16), turned by the heading
> The corners lie at the radius r on the angles heading +/- b and their opposites, so b sets the aspect. Through MulWordByte `$67D9`. The mission vector `$67FA`.
> Witness: L1 2485 (c1, death, missions, play, play2).

$AB7B c BoxRect ; Native (half angle, radius, height): the same rectangle box with 8-bit corners (Sine8, MulFrac)
> The mission vector `$67F7`; the most used box (bank 3 models, mission 1: 22 of 31 models).
> Witness: L1 6221 (c1, controls, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$ABFD b BoxTiltPitch 2 ; Spare byte; the pitch of BoxTilted (`$ABFE`, from the object record +`$2A` by DrawObject `$B827`)

$ABFF c BoxTilted ; Native (half angle, radius, height): a rectangle box turned by the heading, the pitch `$ABFE` and the roll `$68E6`
> Rotates each corner pair with RotatePair `$AD06` (sine and cosine of the roll in `$AD04`); sets V0 = 0. Called from OpNative in death and play2 (a tilted vehicle).
> Witness: L1 0 (death, play2).

$AD04 b RollSinCos 2 ; The sine and cosine of the roll for RotatePair

$AD06 c RotatePair ; Turn the pair (B, C) by the angle in `$AD04`: HL, DE = the two rotated words
> Witness: L1 1563 (death, play2).

@module world ; The world: the mission map (vertices, segments), its visibility, the terrain drawing, the camera
@about The map of a mission lives in its block at bank 0 $DBC5: 64 vertices (X at $DC00+i, Y at $DC40+i, signed bytes, 1024 world units each) and ($DBDC) segments of 6 bytes at $DC80 (vertex a, vertex b, orientation, two sizes, style). SegmentVisibility $AD45 keeps the segments with an endpoint within 8 coarse units of the player; DrawSegments $AEE1 draws them as quads; GroundDots $BAAC draws the ground grid.
$AD45 c SegmentVisibility ; Mark the segments near the player visible, 0 / $FF per segment at $8305
> Sets the coarse player position `$BC12` (X) and `$BC1D` (Y) = the camera words `$67A8` / `$67AB` >> 2, then for each of the ($DBDC) segments at `$DC80` tests both endpoints (TestVertexNear `$AE5C` / `$AE78`): visible if one lies within 8 coarse units on both axes. The flag goes to `$8305`+n. From the segment ($DBDE) on (the switchable ones) the flag is ANDed with the switch flags `$7BFD`, so a gate or bridge destroyed or opened by the mission script disappears.
> Witness: L1 3550 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AE42 c ResetSegmentWalk ; Reset the segment walk: $DC80, the count ($DBDC), the flags $8305
> Stores `$DC80` in the pointer `$AD4C`, the segment count in `$AE5A`, `$8305` in `$AD48` and clears `$AE5B`. Called before SegmentVisibility.
> Witness: L1 3576 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AE5A b SegmentWalkCount 2 ; The segments left in the walk and the walk index
> Written by ResetSegmentWalk `$AE42`.

$AE5C c TestVertexNear ; Test vertex A against the coarse player position: within 8 units
> EXX, then reads vertex X `$DC00`+A against `$BC12`; falls into TestVertexNearX `$AE61`. Carry out: the vertex is near.
> Witness: L1 33063 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AE61 c TestVertexNearX ; Compare one vertex coordinate with the player's, |d| < 8
> Input L = the vertex table offset, A = the player's coarse coordinate. Output carry set when |vertex - player| < 8. Used for both axes (TestVertexNearY `$AE79` adds `$40` to reach the Y table).
> Witness: L1 58209 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AE78 c TestVertexNearB ; Test the segment's second vertex (EXX, then the Y test)
> EXX and falls into TestVertexNearY `$AE79`.
> Witness: L1 24774 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AE79 c TestVertexNearY ; Test a vertex's Y ($DC40+i) against $BC1D
> L = vertex + `$40`, A = (`$BC1D`), then JP TestVertexNearX `$AE61`.
> Witness: L1 25146 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AE82 b SegmentScratch 8 ; 30 bytes of scratch for the segment draw
> Zero in every image; the segment drawing keeps its working values here (the word at `$AE9E` is read by DrawSegmentTail `$B18A`).

$AEA0 c SetupClipWindow ; Build the clip window and the vertex buffers for the segment draw
> From the segment count (+5) sets the loop limit `$AEEA`, the clip window and the vertex buffers at `$FD00`-`$FF07` and `$990F`. Called once per frame before DrawSegments.
> Witness: L1 3507 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AEE1 c DrawSegments ; Draw every visible segment as a quad
> Walks the segments whose flag in `$8305` is set: transforms both vertices (TransformVertex `$B242`), clips them by the orientation byte +2 (one axis `$AFDE`, the other `$B000`, the diagonals `$B021`, `$B0E4`, `$B16A`), and draws the quad by the style byte +5 (DrawSegmentStyle `$B1B6`).
> Witness: L1 36513 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AEE8 c DrawSegmentLoop ; The loop of DrawSegments, entered again by DrawSegmentTail
> One pass per segment: reads the next 6-byte record, skips it when its flag is 0.
> Witness: L1 36513 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$AFDE c ClipSegmentAxisX ; Clip an axis-aligned segment (orientation 0)
> The segment runs along one axis; its width is +3 (`$B2E5`), its height +4 (`$AFC4`). Seen only on the maps of missions 1 and 2 (missions, m2erbe).
> Witness: L1 702 (m2erbe, missions).

$B000 c ClipSegmentAxisY ; Clip a segment along the other axis (orientation bit 7)
> As ClipSegmentAxisX `$AFDE` for the other axis.
> Witness: L1 744 (m2erbe, missions).

$B021 c ClipSegmentDiagonal ; Clip a diagonal segment
> Orientation other than 0 / `$80`: the two vertices give the slope; calls ClipDiagonalSide `$B0E4` and `$B16A`.
> Witness: L1 744 (m2erbe, missions).

$B0E4 c ClipDiagonalSide ; Clip one side of a diagonal segment
> Part of ClipSegmentDiagonal `$B021`.
> Witness: L1 594 (m2erbe, missions).

$B16A c ClipDiagonalEnd ; Clip the far end of a diagonal segment
> Part of ClipSegmentDiagonal `$B021`.
> Witness: L1 2955 (m2erbe, missions).

$B18A c DrawSegmentTail ; Continue the segment loop from the saved pointer $AE9E
> LD HL,(`$AE9E`) then JP DrawSegmentLoop `$AEE8`.
> Witness: L1 6628 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B190 c TransformSegmentEnds ; Transform both corners of a segment into the vertex buffer $FD00
> Points the store `$B2F1` / `$B2F7` at `$FD00` / `$FD06`, transforms the first corner (TransformVertex `$B242`), copies the height `$AFC4` to `$B2E5`, then the second corner into `$FD02` / `$FD04`.
> Witness: L1 6277 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B1B6 c DrawSegmentStyle ; Draw a segment by its style byte (+5)
> ResetViewOrigin `$B3B6`, then the style (the operand at `$B1BA`): 0 draws with IX = `$FF8C`, negative with `$FF80`, 1 with `$FF98`, 2 through `$B22C`, 4 / 5 / 6 set the `$FE00` constants first. The same byte is the terrain type TerrainCollision `$CC3C` returns in `$CE69`.
> Witness: L1 6628 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B242 c TransformVertex ; Transform one map vertex to view space
> Input: the vertex index. Vertex minus camera (VertexRelative `$B265`), the rotation (`$B2FF`, `$B38E`), the stores through `$B2F1` / `$B2F7`.
> Witness: L1 12554 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B265 c VertexRelative ; Vertex position minus the camera, 24-bit
> Byte * 1024 (ByteToWorld `$B282`) minus the camera X / Y `$67A8` / `$67AB`.
> Witness: L1 25108 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B26F c Negate24 ; Negate a 24-bit value
> Seen only in missions (167 runs).
> Witness: L1 167 (missions).

$B27E c VertexByteToWorld ; A vertex byte to a 24-bit world coordinate (signed byte * 1024)
> Reads the vertex byte and falls into ByteToWorld `$B282`.
> Witness: L1 1488 (m2erbe, missions).

$B282 c ByteToWorld ; Signed byte to 24-bit: A * 1024 (vector $67E2)
> Input A, output the 24-bit value in A:HL. The mission code calls it through `$67E2` (the object list's X / Y words use the same scale).
> Witness: L1 35297 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B294 c ClipTestX ; Clip test of a view-space point against the window on X
> Carry out: outside.
> Witness: L1 9467 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B2BB c ClipTestY ; Clip test of a view-space point on Y (depth)
> Carry out: outside.
> Witness: L1 9364 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B2E4 c StoreVertex ; Store a transformed vertex through $B2F1 / $B2F7
> The height operand `$B2E5` (from the segment's +3) is the vertex's height.
> Witness: L1 13256 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B2FF c RotateVertex ; Rotate a camera-relative vertex by the view angle
> Through the camera sin / cos `$9A6C` / `$9A8E`.
> Witness: L1 26512 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B386 c SignExtendA ; Sign-extend A into HL (H = 0 or $FF)
> Seen only in missions.
> Witness: L1 3624 (missions).

$B38E c RotateAndStore ; Rotate by the sin / cos of A and store the pair
> EX AF,AF', sin / cos through `$67E8`, multiply by `$9A8E` (RotateMul `$B3A6`), clears the target.
> Witness: L1 24700 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B3A6 c RotateMul ; One product of the rotation (BC * the sin or cos)
> Part of RotateAndStore.
> Witness: L1 49400 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B3AD c RotateMulAdd ; The second product, added to the first
> Part of RotateAndStore.
> Witness: L1 53024 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B3B6 c ResetViewOrigin ; Reset the view origin before a segment is drawn
> Called by DrawSegmentStyle `$B1B6` once per drawn segment (6628 runs, as many as it).
> Witness: L1 6628 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

@module objects
$B3C9 b WeaponTemplates 30 ; The resident templates of the projectile types $80-$8C: 13 records of 30 bytes from $B3CA
> ObjectSetType `$BD41` copies record (type - `$80`) when the type has bit 7: the 30 bytes become +1..+$1E of the object (flags, colour, height, speed, box, hit points, damage, radius, step handler, collision handler, model, score). `$80` K-40 mortar shell (step `$B5E8`), `$81` cannon shell (`$B592`), `$82` / `$83` Banshee RR / IR, `$84` / `$85` Phoenix, `$86` Dragonfly, `$87` cluster bomb (`$CF4A`), `$88` Sleeper mine, `$89` decoy, `$8A` Phantasm, `$8B` cluster, `$8C` the Helicarrier. The byte at `$B3C9` (`$C9`) is the RET of the routine before.
$B3CA ShellTemplate80 ; template $80, the K-40 mortar shell; 30 bytes a type up to $8C

@module player
$B550 c ConsumeAmmo ; Take one round from the current slot; find a slot for the projectile
> Reads the slot's ammunition pointer (`$B551`, from SelectAmmoPointer `$D3C6`), DEC A and stores it (the Infinite Ammo POKE writes 0 at `$B554`, the DEC A becomes NOP). Returns M when empty. Then FindFreeObject `$BCD6`, the fire sound `$D898`, and prints the count at `$C527`.
> Witness: L1 70 (death, play, play2).
$B554 ; the Infinite Ammo POKE writes 0 here (DEC A becomes NOP)

$B568 c FireCannon ; Fire the turret cannon (store type 4): projectile $81
> Ammunition, then ObjectSetType with `$81`, the position and heading of the player, +31 lifetime.
> Witness: L1 61 (death, play2).

$B592 c CannonShellStep ; Step of a cannon shell: move, lifetime 100
> MoveObject `$BFD1`, counts +$31 down from 100, removes the shell at 0 (RemoveObject `$B8B1`).
> Witness: L1 5682 (death, play2).

$B59F c FireMortar ; Fire the K-40 mortar (store type 3): projectile $80
> SelectAmmoPointer, A = `$80`, then LaunchProjectile `$B5A7`.
> Witness: L1 2 (play).

$B5A7 c LaunchProjectile ; Spawn projectile type A at the player with the aim's elevation
> Input A = the template type (`$80`-`$8B`). ConsumeAmmo `$B550`, ObjectSetType `$BD41`, copies the player's heading and X / Y, the elevation from `$B5C5` / `$B5C8` (SetElevation `$CF32`). Returns M when out of rounds.
> Witness: L1 7 (play, play2).

$B5E8 c MortarShellStep ; Step of a mortar shell: ballistic flight, burst at the ground
> Height += vertical speed (+$31), the speed falls each pass; at height 0 the shell bursts (Explode `$B8AB`).
> Witness: L1 68 (play).

@module enemies ; The resident enemy support: the hit test, kills, debris, the score of a kill
@about The enemies' behaviour is code in the mission block ($E381 on for mission 1, through the vectors $67BE-$67FD); what stays resident is the hit test and the kill: HitTest $B660, the debris, the score of the kill to $68E2-$68E5.
$B611 b NullHandler 1 ; A RET used as a null handler
> The collision handler of objects that ignore collisions; vector `$67EB` points here.

$B612 c KillGunEmplacement ; The collision handler of type $0E (gun emplacement): hit, kill, debris
> HitPoints `$B6B1`; on a kill unregisters the collision (`$67CD`), makes debris (`$67DF`) and joins the common kill path `$B677`. Witness: one kill in death.
> Witness: L1 1 (death).

$B61E b KillSwitchObject 8 ; A collision handler no recording runs: hit, then switch a segment off
> Code: HitTest through `$67DC`; on a kill reads the segment pointer at ($DBDF) and the first switchable index ($DBDE) and clears a switch flag at `$7BFD`, so the bridge or gate it guards vanishes from the map. Reached only through a template's handler word.

$B660 c HitTest ; Damage IX by IY's damage; on a kill score and remove (vector $67DC)
> Input IX = the hit object, IY = the hitter. HitPoints `$B6B1` (+$13 -= the hitter's +$14); no kill returns NC. On a kill: UnregisterCollision `$CA3B`, Debris `$B6D1`; an object from the mission list (+0 != `$FF`) goes to KillMissionObject `$B67D`, the others are freed at `$B677`. Then AddKillScore `$B692`.
> Witness: L1 153 (death, missions, play2).

$B67D c KillMissionObject ; A killed mission object: mark it in the list, leave the wreck
> MarkDestroyed `$B6BD`, sets the wreck bit 6 of +2 (the wreck model +8/+9 is drawn), clears the step handler bit.
> Witness: L1 4 (death).

$B692 c AddKillScore ; Add the object's score (+$1E/+$1F) to the 32-bit score $68E2
> Adds the word to `$68E2`-`$68E5` and calls the kill sound `$D873`. Death: the score goes 0, `$FA`, `$1F4` (two kills of a 250-point type).
> Witness: L1 5 (death).

$B6B1 c HitPoints ; Subtract the hitter's damage from the hit points; carry = killed
> +$13 of IX -= +$14 of IY.
> Witness: L1 7 (death).

$B6BD c MarkDestroyed ; Mark a mission object destroyed in the list (vector $67E5)
> Record ($DBDA) + 8 * (+0): sets bit 1 (destroyed), clears bit 7 (alive), so it is never spawned again. The goal hooks read this bit.
> Witness: L1 4 (death).

$B6D1 c Debris ; Throw 8 debris particles from the object (vector $67DF)
> Fills the bank 3 particle list at `$CFEC` (8 records of 20 bytes): the object's position, random velocities (DebrisVelocity `$B74B` / `$B75C`).
> Witness: L1 13 (death, play2).

$B74B c DebrisVelocity ; A random velocity component for a particle
> Random through `$67D0`.
> Witness: L1 64 (death, play2).

$B75C c DebrisVelocityB ; The second component (shares the code)
> The entry DebrisVelocity's second call uses for the other axis.
> Witness: L1 64 (death, play2).

@module objects
$B766 c BearingTo ; Bearing from IX to IY, a byte angle (vector $67C1)
> dx, dy of the two records, then the octant and the ratio (BearingOctant `$B916`, BearingRatio `$B94A`, the table `$B9DE`). Output A = 0-255.
> Witness: L1 7491 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B7AE c InvertPanelA ; Invert the screen rows of the table $6500 (a panel flash)
> HL = `$6500`, then InvertPanelRows `$B7BD`. Seen in m2erbe, missions and play (12 runs).
> Witness: L1 12 (m2erbe, missions, play).

$B7B6 c InvertPanelB ; Invert the rows of the table $6550
> HL = `$6550` (or the caller's HL), then InvertPanelRows. RefreshWeaponPanel `$C632` calls it with `$6500`.
> Witness: L1 26 (death, play, play2).

$B7BD c InvertPanelRows ; Invert N screen rows from a table of addresses
> Each table entry is a screen address; the row's bytes are complemented (a flash of the panel when a weapon is selected or hit).
> Witness: L1 38 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B7E5 c ScriptDrawCarried ; 3D script opcode 22: draw the carried object when the flag $B7EB is set
> Called from the script interpreter `$990F` (opcode 22, `$98E1` table). Pops the return address into the `JP nn` at `$B824` (operand `$B825`); the operand of `LD A,n` at `$B7EB` is the flag. When it is set: saves `$9A8E` / `$9AB3` / `$9A6C`, pages bank 3 (`$726C`), DrawModel `$B82A` with the record from `$68E6`, restores the view values. In every recording the flag is 0 and only the `JP` back runs.
> Witness: L1 4 (play2).
$B824 ScriptDrawCarriedReturn ; JP nn: the script's return address

$B827 c DrawObject ; Draw one object: its model, or the wreck model
> Input IX = the record. +2 bit 6 picks the wreck model +8/+9 instead of +$1C/+$1D; falls into DrawModel `$B82A`.
> Witness: L1 9194 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B82A c DrawModel ; Project and draw a 3D model at the object's view-space position
> Loads the view x / depth (+$2B..+$2E) into `$9A8E` / `$9AB3`, the night-sight mode `$757A`, and calls the 3D engine (bank 2 `$990F`).
> Witness: L1 9194 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B8A8 b DrawModelTail 3 ; A CALL $C506 no recording runs
> `CALL $C506` (ResetSightTimer) at the end of the routine before; no recording takes that path.

@module player
$B8AB c Explode ; Explode a projectile: debris and the explosion sound
> Debris `$B6D1`, the sound `$D86B`, then RemoveObject.
> Witness: L1 8 (death, play2).

@module objects
$B8B1 c RemoveObject ; Free a record: unregister its collision, clear +2
> Input IX. UnregisterCollision `$CA3B`, +2 = 0 (the slot is free for FindFreeObject).
> Witness: L1 61 (death, play, play2).

@module player
$B8B9 b MortarElevationUp 11 ; Raise the mortar elevation (no recording runs it)
> `LD A,n` / `INC A` / `CP $40` / `RET NC` / `LD ($B8BA),A`: the elevation is the operand at `$B8BA`, 32 at start. Only the down key ran in the recordings.

$B8C4 c MortarElevationDown ; Lower the mortar elevation
> Decrements the elevation `$B8BA` (play: 4 runs, the K-40 aim).
> Witness: L1 4 (play).

$B8CC c ShowMortarRange ; Print the mortar range for the elevation
> Prints the elevation's range in the HUD (play: 5 runs).
> Witness: L1 5 (play).

$B8FC b IrViewHeight 13 ; The height used by the IR view, and its setter
> `$B8FC`-`$B8FD` are spare, `$B8FE` `LD HL,0` (its operand `$B8FF` the IR camera height), `$B901` adds 8 and stores it: raise the IR view. AimLimit `$B909` lowers it.

$B909 c AimLimit ; Clamp the aim within the weapon's limit
> `$B8FF` -= 8 unless it would go below 0 (play2: 5 runs). Lowers the camera of the IR view (Banshee IRSS).
> Witness: L1 5 (play2).

@module objects
$B916 c BearingOctant ; BearingTo: the octant from the signs of dx, dy
> dx, dy signs give 8 octants; then BearingRatio.
> Witness: L1 7491 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B94A c BearingRatio ; BearingTo: the ratio of the smaller to the larger delta
> Divides the smaller |delta| by the larger to an index of BearingTable.
> Witness: L1 7491 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B95A c BearingLookup ; BearingTo: the angle from the table $B9DE
> Adds the octant base to the table angle.
> Witness: L1 7491 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$B9DE b BearingTable 8 ; The arctangent table of BearingTo
> 24 bytes of angles read by BearingLookup `$B95A`.

@module world
$B9F6 c SetCamera ; Set the camera from the viewed object (the player, a missile, the Dragonfly)
> Copies +$21..+$28 (table select, heading, X, Y) of the record at (`$B9F4`) to `$67A5`-`$67AC`, the height +5/+6 (or the IR height `$B8FF` when `$BA13` is set) to `$67AD`. The rear view (`$BA27` set) adds `$80` to the heading. Then CameraSinCos `$BA32`.
> Witness: L1 3550 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BA32 c CameraSinCos ; The camera heading's sine and cosine
> Reads the camera heading `$67A6`, sin / cos through `$67E8` (`$A899`), stores the pair in the operands `$BBBD` / `$BBC8` of RotateToView.
> Witness: L1 7100 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BA40 c CameraSinCosAgain ; CameraSinCos for the second pass
> CALL CameraSinCos for the second view pass.
> Witness: L1 3550 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BA45 c RearViewOff ; Rear view off
> Clears `$BA27`, falls into ToggleRearView.
> Witness: L1 5 (play).

$BA4A c ToggleRearView ; Rear view on or off: the flag $BA27, the text REAR:VIEW / :::
> Prints `$BA86` ("REAR:VIEW") or `$BA9F` (blank) with the attribute at `$5AD2`.
> Witness: L1 31 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BA6E b ViewTexts 13 ; The view labels: IR:SIGHT, REAR:VIEW, BINOC:X2 and their blanks
> Strings for PrintString `$6FB3` (`$07` position code, `$FF` end): `$BA6E` "IR:SIGHT", `$BA7A` blank, `$BA86` "REAR:VIEW", `$BA93` "BINOC:X2" (the digit at `$BA9D`), `$BA9F` blank.
$BA7A IrSightBlank
$BA86 RearViewText ; "REAR:VIEW"
$BA93 BinocularText ; "BINOC:X2", the digit at $BA9D set by ShowBinocularZoom
$BA9F ViewTextBlank

$BAAC c GroundDots ; Draw the ground-plane dot grid
> The grid moves with the camera: GridVectors `$BB54`, then PlotGroundDot `$BB75` for each dot, GridStep `$BBA6` between rows.
> Witness: L1 3507 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BB54 c GridVectors ; The grid's step vectors for the camera heading
> The camera's sin / cos scaled to the grid spacing: the steps along a row and between rows.
> Witness: L1 14028 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BB75 c PlotGroundDot ; Project one ground dot and plot it
> Rotates the dot to view space, divides by depth, plots through `$AA27` when on screen (117 517 runs).
> Witness: L1 117517 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BBA6 c GridStep ; Step to the next grid row
> Adds the row vector to the grid origin.
> Witness: L1 7014 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BBBC c RotateToView ; Rotate dx, dy by the camera (sin `$BBBD`, cos `$BBC8`)
> Outputs the view x in `$9A6C` and the depth in `$9A8E`.
> Witness: L1 50296 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

@module objects
$BBF0 b ActivateIndexSave 1 ; Saved operand of ActivateMissionObjects
> The byte before ActivateMissionObjects; its index operands are `$BBF2` / `$BBFA`.

$BBF1 c ActivateMissionObjects ; Spawn the mission objects near the player, despawn the far ones (16 per call)
> Walks the ($DBD9) records of 8 bytes at ($DBDA), 16 per call (the index is kept in `$BBF2` / `$BBFA`). A live record (bit 7) not yet spawned within 9 coarse units (InRange `$BD67`) gets a slot (FindSlot `$BCFD`), its type (ObjectSetType `$BD41`), a collision slot (`$C957`), its heading and position (CopyHeading `$BCBA`, CopyPosition `$BCC6`), and bit 6. A spawned one out of range is freed (bit 6 cleared; the slot found by +0 = the index in `$BC33`).
> Witness: L1 3550 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BCBA c CopyHeading ; Copy the list record's heading (+2) to the object
> The list record's +2 to the object's +$22.
> Witness: L1 183 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BCC6 c CopyPosition ; Copy the list record's X / Y words, << 2 into 24 bits (WordToWorld $BD83)
> +4/+5 and +6/+7 of the list record through WordToWorld `$BD83` to +$23-+$25 and +$26-+$28.
> Witness: L1 366 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BCD6 c FindProjectileSlot ; Find a free record for a projectile (up to record 23)
> D = `$17`, falls into FindFreeObject.
> Witness: L1 70 (death, play, play2).

$BCDA c FindFreeObject ; Find a free record 1-20 (vector $67C4)
> D = `$15`; carry set and IX = the record when found.
> Witness: L1 219 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BCDC c FindFreeObjectD ; Find a free record below D: +2 = 0
> Stores 23 - E in `$C95C` and the record in `$C973`.
> Witness: L1 289 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BCF0 c FindFreeLoop ; The scan loop
> Steps 60 bytes per record until +2 = 0 or the limit.
> Witness: L1 415 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BCFD c FindSlot ; Find a slot for a list record
> FindFreeObject `$BCDA`, then the list index to +0.
> Witness: L1 185 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BD41 c ObjectSetType ; Set the type and copy the 30-byte template (vector $67C7)
> Input A = type. Bit 7: the resident template `$B3CA` + 30 * (A - `$80`); else the mission's template table (`$DBD7`) + 30 * A. Copies to +1..+$1E and sets the serial +$20.
> Witness: L1 431 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BD67 c InRange ; Is the list record within 9 coarse units of the player
> |X word >> 8 - `$BC12`| and |Y - `$BC1D`| below 9. Called for each list record (70 373 runs).
> Witness: L1 70373 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BD83 c WordToWorld ; A list word << 2 into a 24-bit coordinate
> HL << 2 with the carry into the third byte.
> Witness: L1 366 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BD98 c TransformObjects ; Make every present object camera-relative, cull it, insert it into the depth tree
> For each record with +2 bit 7: position minus camera, RotateToView `$BBBC`, depth cull, OnScreen `$BEA2` with the radius, then DepthInsert `$BEDE` into the tree at `$6800`; a blip for the radar (RadarAddBlip `$C0B2`).
> Witness: L1 3550 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BEA2 c OnScreen ; Is the object within the screen with its radius
> View x (+$2B/+$2C) against the depth with the radius +$16/+$17.
> Witness: L1 32872 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BEA8 c OnScreenX ; The x half of OnScreen
> The entry for the x test.
> Witness: L1 32885 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BED2 c ClearDepthTree ; Empty the depth tree at $6800
> Resets the node pointer and the root at `$6800`.
> Witness: L1 3550 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BEDE c DepthInsert ; Insert a record into the depth tree (6-byte nodes: depth, left, right, record)
> Walks from the root, left when nearer, right when farther, and links a new 6-byte node.
> Witness: L1 9829 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BF20 b DepthTreeVars 4 ; Variables of the depth tree
> Zero in the image; the walk of the tree keeps its stack depth here.

@module player
$BF24 c FindMissileTarget ; Search the depth tree for a missile target
> Returns at once when `$66D4` is 0; else walks the nodes at `$6800` (the target search of TargetInCone `$C197`).
> Witness: L1 8 (play, play2).

@module objects
$BF53 c DrawObjectsInOrder ; Draw the objects far to near (in-order walk of the depth tree)
> Calls DrawEntry `$BF83` per node.
> Witness: L1 3507 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BF83 c DrawEntry ; Draw one tree entry: an object (DrawObject) or a debris particle
> A pointer at or above `$CF00` is a particle of the bank 3 list, drawn as a dot.
> Witness: L1 9715 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$BFD1 c MoveObject ; Move an object by its speed along its heading (vector $67BE)
> X += speed * sin(heading), Y += speed * cos(heading), through `$A8B2` / `$A7F2`.
> Witness: L1 14450 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C026 c RunObjectHandlers ; Run each present object's step handler
> 24 records from `$75F0`: when +2 bit 7 and +3 bit 0 are set, CALL (+$18) with IX = the record.
> Witness: L1 3550 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C05E c DrawRadar ; Draw the radar: clear it, plot the blip list $6768
> ClearRadar `$C094`, then RadarPlotList `$C079` (3483 runs, every 3D frame but the first).
> Witness: L1 3483 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C079 c RadarPlotList ; Plot the list of blips and reset it
> Resets the list pointer `$7BFB`, sets `$AA1A`, plots each pair at `$6768` through PlotRadarPixel `$A9FE`.
> Witness: L1 3483 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C094 c ClearRadar ; Clear 32 rows of 5 bytes at $5036 with stack pushes
> SP = the radar's screen rows, PUSH of zeros (32 rows, 5 bytes each at `$5036`).
> Witness: L1 3483 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C0B2 c RadarAddBlip ; Add an object to the radar list when within range
> Input: the object's offset from the player. RadarRange `$C104`, RadarScale `$C0D2`, RadarStoreBlip `$C0F7`.
> Witness: L1 27405 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C0D2 c RadarScale ; Scale the offsets to radar units
> SRA H / RR L 8 times on each offset.
> Witness: L1 27405 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C0F7 c RadarStoreBlip ; Store the blip in the list at ($7BFB)
> Writes y, x to (`$7BFB`) and advances it.
> Witness: L1 14952 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$C104 c RadarRange ; Is the offset within the radar's range
> Carry set when the offset is out of the radar (|d| beyond the window).
> Witness: L1 48723 (death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

@module player
$C113 b WeightText 8 ; A print of the weight and its text
