@module sound ; The AY driver: the register shadow, the engine tone, the effect counters
@about The AY registers are kept in a 14-byte shadow at $D674 and written every frame by WriteAY $D7DC (select at $FFFD, data at $BFFD). SoundFrame $D692 runs from the interrupt ($7E6E): the engine tone from the speed, then the effect counters set by the one-shot triggers $D84E-$D898.
$D692 c SoundFrame ; The sound step of a frame (the interrupt)
> Gated by `$D691` / `$D689`. EngineTone `$D8A1` from |`$75F7`|, then each effect counter `$D682`-`$D68B` counts down and sets its registers in the shadow `$D674`-`$D681`, then WriteAY `$D7DC` (B = `$FF` select port `$FFFD` at `$D7E4`, data port `$BFFD` at `$D7EB`). Called by the interrupt's `$7E6E` in every recording.
> Witness frames (first-last frame of the recording, runs): c1 24005-33298 (4124), controls 0-330 (242), death 0-20038 (12655), m10 0-9028 (6434), m2erbe 0-7808 (3094), m2ocean 0-4799 (2244), menu 0-10996 (7559), missions 0-35997 (12811), play 0-10930 (5510), play2 0-23665 (12957), search 0-5043 (2265).
> Witness: L1 65529 (death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$D7F4 c SetNoise ; Set the noise period and enable it
> A >> 1 as the noise period when below the current `$D688`; `$D67E` / `$D67A` and the mixer bit 5 (death, play2).
> Witness frames (first-last frame of the recording, runs): c1 32619-33091 (107), death 8122-18058 (896), play2 8608-17213 (553).
> Witness: L1 1449 (death, play2).

$D807 c SilenceAY ; Silence the AY
> Zeroes the 21 bytes from `$D674`, mixer `$3F` (all off), writes the 14 registers.
> Witness frames (first-last frame of the recording, runs): c1 23974-24603 (2), controls 95-264 (2), m2erbe 7454-7522 (2), menu 95-1874 (4), missions 7955-34068 (16), play 10627-10693 (2), play2 9615-23533 (6).
> Witness: L1 30 (m2erbe, menu, missions, play, play2).

